===Etymology 1===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*h₃reǵ-}}
{{dercat|en|gmw-pro|inh=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|reȝt}}, {{m|enm|right}}, {{m|enm|righte}}, {{m|enm|riht}}, {{m|enm|riȝt}}, {{m|enm|riȝte}}, {{m|enm|ryght}}, {{m|enm|ryȝt}}, from {{inh|en|ang|reht}}, {{m|ang|reoht}}, {{m|ang|rieht}}, {{m|ang|riht}}, {{m|ang|ryht|t=right,” also the word for “straight” and “direct}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*reht}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*rehtaz|t=right, straight; just, morally upright}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*h₃reǵtós|t=right, straightened}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*h₃reǵ-|t=to straighten; to righten}}.

The Germanic adjective which has been used also as a noun since the common Germanic period. 
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|sco|richt|t=right}}, {{cog|yol|reights}}, {{m|yol|rights|t=rights}}, {{cog|frr|recht}}, {{m|frr|rocht}}, {{m|frr|rucht|t=right}}, {{cog|stq|gjucht|t=right}}, {{cog|fy|rjocht|t=straight}}, {{cog|gmw-cfr|rääch|t=right}}, {{cog|nl|recht|t=straight}}, {{cog|de|recht}}, {{m|de|Recht|t=right}}, {{cog|li|réët|t=right}}, {{cog|lb|Recht}}, {{m|lb|riets|t=right}}, {{m|lb|riicht|t=straight}}, {{cog|yi|רעכט|t=right}}, {{cog|da|ret|t=right}}, {{cog|fo|rættur|t=right}}, {{cog|is|réttur|t=right}}, {{cog|nb,nn|rett|t=right}}, {{cog|sv|rät|t=straight}}, {{m|sv|rätt|t=right}}, {{cog|got|𐍂𐌰𐌹𐌷𐍄𐍃|t=straight; correct}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of {{cog|br|reiñ|t=to give}}, {{cog|kw|ri|t=to give; to grant; to present}}, {{cog|ga|reachd}}, {{m|ga|reacht|t=law, statute; authority; dispensation}}, {{cog|gd|reachd|t=law, right; command, power}}, {{cog|cy|rhoddi}}, {{m|cy|rhoi|t=to give; to put}}, {{cog|la|rēctus|t=led straight along; correct, right; just, lawful}}, {{cog|grc|ὀρεκτός|t=stretched out; longed for}}, {{cog|lv|redzēt|t=to see}}, {{cog|lt|regėti|t=to see, view}}, {{cog|ae|𐬆𐬭𐬆𐬰𐬎|t=straight}}, {{cog|bal|راست|tr=rást|t=right}}, {{cog|ckb|ڕاست|t=right; straight}}, {{cog|kmr|rast|t=straight; right; true; erect; direct}}, {{cog|os|раст|t=honest, true; correct; exact; straight; fair; direct}}, {{cog|fa|راس|tr=rās / râs}}, {{m|fa|راست|tr=râst|t=straight; direct; true; erect}}, {{cog|zza|raşt|t=right; straight}}, {{cog|sa|ऋजु|t=straight; honest, sincere}}.
