|passage=''Kirsty:'' I suppose you're hungry. Would you like something to eat?<br>''Ken:'' No. I'm '''right''', thanks.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=Catherine Menagé|title=Access to English|publisher=National Centre for English Language Teaching and Research, NSW: Sydney|page=25
|passage=When the sales assistant sees the customer, she asks ''Are you '''right''', sir?'' This means ''Are you all right?'' She wants to know if he needs any help.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2001|author=Morris Gleitzman|title=Two weeks with the Queen|publisher=Pan Macmillan Australia|page=75
|passage='You lost?'<br>Colin spun round. Looking at him was a nurse, her eyebrows raised. / 'No, I'm '''right''', thanks,' said Colin.'}}
